@startuml

start

:Avionics stack (FMS/FADEC) operates on deterministic RTOS;
:High-frequency ISRs manage control law execution;
:Lower-priority worker tasks process;

if (Sensor A reports anomaly?) then (yes)
  if (Altitude > 10,000 feet and Air pressure substandard?) then (yes)
    :Trigger fault condition;
    :Initiate emergency processing module;

    :Perform environmental data acquisition at preset frequency;
    :Apply digital filter in real-time via ring buffer;
    :Condition incoming stream;

    if (Multiple submodules require synchronized activation?) then (yes)
      :Initialize engine monitoring unit;

      :Critical tasks;
      fork
        :Cooling system diagnostics;
      fork again
        :Fuel pressure monitoring;
      end fork

      :Dispatch as concurrent,preemptible threads under RTOS scheduler;
      fork
      :Managed by priority queue;
      fork again
      :Protected by mutexes for shared resource access;
      end fork
    else (no)
    end if

    :Real-time analysis;
    if (Any parameter breaches safety envelope?) then (yes)
      :Trigger alarm subsystem immediately;
      :Log event with CRC-verified fault code;
      :Uplink to ground control center via CAN bus;
      :Use exponential backoff retry mechanism for communication assurance;
    else (no)
    end if
  else (no)
  end if
else (no)
end if

fork
  :Watchdog timer supervises all active tasks;
fork again
  :Fault-tolerant strategies ensure deterministic recovery and data integrity;
end fork

:All software processes adhere to DO-178C/DO-254 design assurance levels;
:Ensure deterministic response and data integrity;

stop

